  "title": "Google, Microsoft, Anthropic, OpenAI moving to support new robots.txt user-agent for AI training opt-out",
  "content": "X author: @vanessafox\n\nGoogle, Microsoft, Anthropic, and OpenAI are working toward supporting (targeting early 2027) a new shared user-agent standard in robots.txt proposed by Anthropic's Kevin Kelley at the IETF, allowing sites to block content use for AI training.\n\nLinked sources:\n- https://www.vanessafox.com/complete-reference-blocking-llm-crawlers/#new-shared-standard-usage-ai-training-in-robots-txt",
